<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef uneven on light demand and light to moderate, offerings. Select chuck and round cuts were steady to firm, while rib and loin cuts firm.  Choice chuck and round cuts steady to weak, while rib and loin cuts steady to firm. Beef trimmings were generally steady on light to moderate demand and offerings. - USDA</p>
<p> 174 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>  48 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>34 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values	  104.24	103.59	 99.02	 98.60</p>
<p>		    0.19	  0.06	  0.21	  0.24</p>
<p>Rib	  154.72	154.63	143.69	143.14</p>
<p>Chuck	 70.95	 67.33	 71.80	 69.28</p>
<p>Round	 94.50	 94.50	 92.99	 92.99</p>
<p>Loin	 165.36	167.39	146.19	148.05</p>
<p>Brisket     64.39	 64.39	 67.15	 67.15</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  65.32	 65.25	 65.55	 65.39</p>
<p>Flank	 58.35	 58.35	 57.91	 57.91</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
